From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui: Windows.Graphics.Display.DisplayInformation

DisplayInformation did not exist. React Native for Windows (OneDrive's interface) asks DisplayInformation.GetForCurrentView for the scale it lays out with, and OneDrive ended with an unhandled exception. It now reports the primary monitor: logical DPI, raw DPI from its physical size, the resolution scale, orientation, raw pixels per view pixel and its size, one object per thread; the events are accepted.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windows.ui/Makefile.in b/dlls/windows.ui/Makefile.in
index 2b0e1bc..337f3e7 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.ui/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/windows.ui/Makefile.in
@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@ SOURCES = \
 	colors_classes.idl \
 	corewindow.c \
 	dispatcher.c \
+	display.c \
+	display_classes.idl \
 	thread_corewindow.c \
 	toast_classes.idl \
 	xmldom_classes.idl \
diff --git a/dlls/windows.ui/display.c b/dlls/windows.ui/display.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..09a710d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/windows.ui/display.c
@@ -0,0 +1,408 @@
+/*
